#
# Counter-example for math:ONNXIngestSourceIdentifiedConstraint: a math:ONNXIngestRun
# whose math:parseSource witness inlines text but names NO math:sourceDigest. An ONNX
# model is blob-scale BINARY held by reference and is never inlined, so the digest — not
# a retained literal — is the only record of WHICH byte stream the protobuf reader
# accepted; a run naming none points at no decoded stream, which is the graph-side
# residue of the front-end's math:MalformedONNXWireFormat refusal.
#
# The polarity is the mirror of the R and TSTP twins: here the RETAINED literal is what
# discharges the shared math:IngestSourceHeldConstraint, leaving only the ONNX-specific
# identify-your-bytes obligation firing. The run carries the full grounding frame and
# produced a codomain. It fires math:ONNXIngestSourceIdentifiedConstraint
# (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent → math:MalformedONNXWireFormat).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/onnx-ingest-source-unidentified/> .

ex:run a math:ONNXIngestRun ;
    math:parseSource ex:srcWitness ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema ex:schema ;
    logic:instantiatesPlan ex:plan ;
    math:ingestCorrespondence ex:corr .

# Inlined text standing in for a binary model — held, but not IDENTIFIED.
ex:srcWitness a math:MathematicalObject ; logic:loadBearing true ;
    math:retainedSource "ir_version: 8 graph { name: \"g\" }" .

ex:schema a logic:ActionSchema .
ex:plan a logic:Plan .
ex:corr a logic:Correspondence ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:LossyLens ;
    logic:mnemomorphic true .

ex:lifted a math:MathematicalObject ; gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ex:run .
